# Floor-presence39 execution scope

The frozen runtime preparation README overstates the inherited controller's
evidence gates. This note records the actual reviewed scope before target
materialization or execution. Preparation01 and the completed host/qualifier
bytes remain unchanged.

The isolated raw fixture uses the inherited nine-command controller. Its QEMU
command has serial stdio, snapshot storage, no NIC, no host audio and
`-no-reboot`. It does not use QMP. The controller checks actual child terminals,
the selected source snapshots, SDK identity, setup compile macros, declared
build-output hashes and the complete packet/PCM protocol. The separate numeric
reader verifies its implemented receipts, frozen inputs, compile macros,
protocol, complete output streams and both actual reference streams.

There is no new full configured dependency walk. The numeric reader does not
independently rehash every reported tool, build output or variant source. Do
not describe this execution as satisfying those additional gates or as proving
production radio startup, physical behavior, performance or full G6 conformance.
The project comparison bound remains 2 signed S16 LSB for every original sample
against each reference, with all predeclared silence/nonzero witnesses retained.

Host39/78 and the recorded qualifier have completed with actual terminal0.
Target capture and target numerical comparison are pending at this note's creation.
